**Claim-style formulation:**

A method for controlling a powertrain of a motor vehicle, the powertrain comprising an internal combustion engine and a forward clutch selectively coupling the internal combustion engine to a driven portion of a transmission, the method comprising:

- in response to determining that a sailing operating condition is present, disengaging the forward clutch and stopping operation of the internal combustion engine;
- while the vehicle remains in motion, detecting a driver-requested acceleration;  
- in response to detecting the driver-requested acceleration, restarting the internal combustion engine and controlling a rotational speed of an input side of the forward clutch toward a rotational speed of an output side of the forward clutch; and
- engaging the forward clutch in response to determining that a difference between the rotational speed of the input side and the rotational speed of the output side is less than a predetermined synchronization threshold.
